        "title": "Weighted ellipsoid class for sequence inversion",
        "statement": "Let $Q\\in[0,\\infty)$ and let $a=(a_j)_{j\\in\\mathbb N}$ be a nondecreasing sequence of positive real numbers, so $0<a_1\\le a_2\\le\\cdots$. The statistical ellipsoid of radius $Q$ and weights $a$ in the Gaussian sequence inverse model is\n$$\\Theta_a(Q)=\\left\\{\\theta\\in\\ell^2(\\mathbb N,\\mathbb R):\\sum_{j=1}^{\\infty}a_j^2\\theta_j^2\\le Q^2\\right\\}.$$\nNo assumption that $a_j\\to\\infty$ is included. In particular, this definition does not assert that the ellipsoid is compact in $\\ell^2$.",
